<title>USA: Enron, Portland to resume Ore. talks.</title>
<headline>Enron, Portland to resume Ore. talks.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Settlement talks between staff of the Oregon Public Utility Commission (OPUC), Enron Corp and Portland General Corp may resume Feb 25, but a final vote on the companies' merger is unlikely by mid-March as had been expected, sources involved in the matter said Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;March 17 seems unrealistic to me because of all the changes we have had,&quot; said Tom Riordan, senior OPUC analyst.</p>
<p>He explained the date was set by the commission as a decision deadline, but that staff has yet to present a final review of the merger and a reply comment period must be observed.</p>
</text>
